{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>הלה היא</b> written with a heh — there will come one who reigned ל\"ה (thirty-five) years, and he is the fifth generation: Salmon, Boaz, Obed, Jesse, David, and he took these cities. Another interpretation: hints at Moses, who was ה\"א ה\"א אמה (five by five cubits), and skipped י' (ten) cubits, and his weapon י' (ten) cubits, and struck him at the ankles, which is י' (ten) cubits."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The word הלה is written with a final heh instead of the expected הלז; Ba'al HaTurim reads הל\"ה as the numerical value 35, alluding to David's 35-year reign over all Israel."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:39.798572119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}